{{document_facts}}

RULES
A. Go through the documents one by one, in the order listed. For each, offer its first date. A date the policyholder names is accepted if the CALENDAR says OK for that document; a weekend or holiday becomes the next business day; a later date: offer the latest due date instead.
B. A document they cannot or will not send ends with a reason: not_available, refused or already_sent.
C. If the list includes a repair estimate, offer an adjuster visit. {{adjuster_window}}
D. When every document has a date or a reason: say "To confirm:" and read all dates (and the visit) back together, then ask "Do you confirm?". After a clear yes, call transition_to_record. If no document has a date, call transition_to_record without a read-back.
Never use the word registered in this step.

